# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the Cloud Build source context.
#
# This file exists because of a real break. Without it, gcloud DERIVES the
# upload filter from .gitignore — so .gitignore silently becomes a fifth
# definition of "what the build sees", alongside source, dist/, .dockerignore
# and the image. Adding package-lock.json to .gitignore for unrelated reasons
# removed it from the build context and the image build died on
# `COPY failed: stat package-lock.json: file does not exist`.
#
# Stating the context explicitly means .gitignore can never change what ships
# again. Keep this narrow: .dockerignore does the fine-grained filtering once
# the context arrives.
.git/
.gitignore
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
coverage/
**/coverage/
.turbo/
.cache/
.next/
*.log
.venv/
__pycache__/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.local/
instagram-output/
.media-cache/
